      "mergeID": "6757554f5cb99a5eb2b9cccc",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Seems like you can get an instance in a weird state where it appears like the other player has blocked you. The person that join last can see the other person. And not the other way around. My friend could see me as if I've blocked him since he was the instance owner. When I was the one not seeing him I could not have guessed that he was there.\n\nSeems like the API outside of the client can see him in the same instance.\n\nUDON still synced as expected. \n\nWhen we eventually tried to go over to another instance everything was back to normal again.\n\nOther user was using live version 1458.\n\nLog: https://gist.github.com/Tummy-git/b13f7ccba4d2e40a1cf22aedc372fa94\n\nVideo showing problem: https://youtu.be/FL4OZJK4cW8",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1468] Not being able to see other user.",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6755c32e30a7a189bb3b448f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The same has been happening to me quite often with the last 2-3 versions. Happens in live, but also on the current open beta (2024.2.3, build 1468).  For me however, my friend does usually appear in the \"in room\" list, and vice versa. \n\nThere doesn't seem to be any particular condition that causes it. It seems pretty random, so may be hard to recreate.  Rejoining the world usually fixes it.  I do wonder how many times people may have thought I was ignoring them, when I just couldn't see them...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
